messages:
lisa.devex: Heads-up — samples/weatherbot README has an out-of-date streaming example that breaks for people on SDK v1.4. The snippet uses `client.stream()` and an async-iterator shape that no longer exists. Saw two new hires hit this during onboarding this morning.

sam.engineer: ugh, thanks for flagging. can you paste the exact failing snippet?

lisa.devex: sure — here's the copy/paste that people hit: 

```js
const resp = await client.stream({ model: 'redwood-alpha', input: prompt });
for await (const chunk of resp) {
  process.stdout.write(chunk.text);
}
```

lisa.devex: error they see: `TypeError: resp[Symbol.asyncIterator] is not a function` or `client.stream is not a function`. also package.json in the sample pins `@redwood/sdk": "1.2.0"` so the README and the installed SDK are out of sync.

toni.docs: thanks — that explains it. the API changed in 1.3 -> `client.streamMessages()` returns an object with `.iter()` for the async iterator (or you can use `for await (const msg of resp.iter())`). we should update both the README and package.json in the sample.

sam.engineer: proposed fixed snippet to replace the block above: 

```js
// new SDK shape (v1.4+)
const streamResp = await client.streamMessages({ model: 'redwood-alpha', input: prompt });
for await (const msg of streamResp.iter()) {
  // msg has { delta, role, text } depending on model
  process.stdout.write(msg.text ?? '');
}
```

sam.engineer: also add a tiny migration note: "If you copied an earlier streaming example that used `client.stream()` you may need to upgrade `@redwood/sdk` to ^1.3.0 and switch to `streamMessages()` / `.iter()`."

toni.docs: I'll open a PR to update README, bump the sample's package.json to `^1.4.0`, and add a one-line migration callout. Should we also add a unit smoke test in CI that runs the sample with a local stub so this doesn't regress?

lisa.devex: yes please — a smoke test would catch copy/paste drift. test can import the sample's `run()` and assert it yields at least one message when run against the SDK stub. keep it lightweight.

sam.engineer: created branch `devex/streaming-readme-fix` and draft PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/samples/pull/412 (WIP). includes README update + package bump + a CI smoke job that runs `node smoke.js` (stubbed).

deploy-bot: PR #412 created by sam.engineer — check CI status: pending. :rocket:

toni.docs: once CI passes, i'll merge and add a tiny changelog entry in samples/CHANGES.md noting the API rename for onboarding docs. also will add a short line in the onboarding checklist so SREs know to update pinned sample deps before cohort starts.

lisa.devex: perfect. one more small ask — add a short line to the README showing the exact error message people will see when they hit the old copy/paste (`client.stream is not a function`) so it's easier to search and triage. saved me 10 minutes today. :sweat_smile: 

sam.engineer: added that to the PR. :+1:

toni.docs: merged and published sample at v0.3.1 — changed README + package bump + smoke CI. I'll follow up in #onboarding with the migration note.

lisa.devex: awesome, thanks everyone. this small fix will reduce a lot of onboarding friction. :tada:
